          "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
          "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 10 at 12:19AM PST until November 10 at 12:00PM PST by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Minor",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...Up to 1.6 ft of inundation above ground level is\npossible in low-lying areas near shorelines and tidal\nwaterways.\n\n* WHERE...Coastal North Bay Including Point Reyes National\nSeashore, San Francisco Peninsula Coast and Northern Monterey\nBay.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon PST today.\n\n* IMPACTS...High tides will result in flooding of low-lying\ninfrastructure, isolated road closures, and coastal erosion.\nRising tides will bring water and waves farther up the beach\nthan normal, restricting escape from beaches and coastal areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...At the San Francisco tide gauge, high tide\nis expected to be: 1.5 ft above normal (7.3 ft MLLW) at 11:04\nAM Tuesday 11/10, 1.4 ft above normal (7.2 ft MLLW) at 11:35 AM\nWednesday 11/11, 1.3 ft above normal (7.1 ft MLLW) at 12:10 PM\nThursday 11/12, 1.1 ft above normal (6.9 ft MLLW) at 12:49 PM\nFriday 11/13. These predictions include up to 1.4 ft of surge\nthat will enhance the astronomical tide and flooding threat.\nHigh tide varies up to 90 minutes earlier or later along the\nPacific Coast and through the San Francisco Bay, respectively.",
          "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
          "expires": "2026-11-10T12:00:00-08:00",
          "source_url": "https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.863a5bb8f453b4254cd1f62100528b3c170da4b2.003.1"
